# Resonite ProtoFlux — the in-world node-graph runtime.
#
# Rung 0: the ~40 node types a rung-0 FBD emitter reaches to lower a
# RECTGTN plan into a ProtoFlux graph a Resonite session executes.
# Source of truth: `wiki.resonite.com` ProtoFlux node reference
# (CC-BY-4.0, retrieved Aug 2026); node fully-qualified names taken
# from Resonite's own `FrooxEngine.ProtoFlux.*` C# assembly namespaces
# as documented publicly.
#
# ProtoFlux distinguishes IMPULSE (flow) sockets and VALUE sockets, same
# as KHR_interactivity. A `*` socket means variadic.
#
# Format: `<Namespace>/<Node>  <impulse-in> // <value-in> -> <impulse-out> // <value-out>`

# ---- lifecycle (graph entry points) ------------------------------

Runtime/OnStart                                    _  //  _  -> Fire  //  _
Runtime/Update                                     _  //  _  -> Fire  //  DeltaSeconds
Runtime/UpdateWithDelta                            _  //  _  -> Fire  //  Delta
Runtime/DynamicImpulseReceiver                     _  //  Tag  -> Fire  //  Data
Runtime/DynamicImpulseTrigger                      Trigger  //  Tag, Data  -> OnDone  //  _

# ---- flow control (GRAFCET step + transition mapping) ------------

Flow/Sequence                                      In  //  _  -> Then0, Then1, Then2  //  _
Flow/If                                            In  //  Condition  -> True, False  //  _
Flow/While                                         In  //  Condition  -> LoopIteration, Done  //  _
Flow/For                                           In  //  Start, End, Step  -> LoopIteration, Done  //  CurrentIndex
Flow/PulseDelay                                    In  //  Delay  -> DelayedPulse  //  _
Flow/OneShot                                       In  //  _  -> OnFirst, OnLater  //  _

# ---- booleans + comparisons --------------------------------------

Bool/AND_Bool                                      _  //  A, B  -> _  //  *
Bool/OR_Bool                                       _  //  A, B  -> _  //  *
Bool/NOT_Bool                                      _  //  A  -> _  //  *
Bool/XOR_Bool                                      _  //  A, B  -> _  //  *
Math/Equals_T                                      _  //  A, B  -> _  //  *
Math/LessThan_T                                    _  //  A, B  -> _  //  *
Math/LessOrEqual_T                                 _  //  A, B  -> _  //  *

# ---- arithmetic --------------------------------------------------

Math/ValueAdd_T                                    _  //  A, B  -> _  //  *
Math/ValueSub_T                                    _  //  A, B  -> _  //  *
Math/ValueMul_T                                    _  //  A, B  -> _  //  *
Math/ValueDiv_T                                    _  //  A, B  -> _  //  *
Math/Sin_Float                                     _  //  N  -> _  //  *
Math/Cos_Float                                     _  //  N  -> _  //  *
Math/Clamp_T                                       _  //  Value, Min, Max  -> _  //  *
Math/Lerp_T                                        _  //  A, B, Alpha  -> _  //  *

# ---- variables + fields on scene slots ---------------------------

References/ValueRead_T                             _  //  Source  -> _  //  *
References/ValueWrite_T                            Write  //  Target, Value  -> OnDone  //  _
Slots/GetPosition                                  _  //  Slot  -> _  //  Position
Slots/SetPosition                                  Write  //  Slot, Position  -> OnDone  //  _
Slots/GetRotation                                  _  //  Slot  -> _  //  Rotation
Slots/SetRotation                                  Write  //  Slot, Rotation  -> OnDone  //  _
Slots/GetActive_Self                               _  //  Slot  -> _  //  Active
Slots/SetActive_Self                               Write  //  Slot, Active  -> OnDone  //  _

# ---- users + networking ------------------------------------------

Users/LocalUser                                    _  //  _  -> _  //  User
Users/AllUsers                                     _  //  _  -> _  //  Users
Users/IsUserPresent                                _  //  User  -> _  //  Present

# ---- rule for the emitter ----------------------------------------
# SR_L -> References/ValueWrite_Bool driven by an OR of Set / Clear
# `PulseDelay` impulses. AND / OR / NOT compose Bool nodes directly.
# TON lowers to `Flow/PulseDelay` with the preset as `Delay`. MOVE
# becomes `Slots/SetPosition` or `References/ValueWrite_T` depending
# on the destination type. Nothing else lowers cleanly at rung 0.
